#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:22
msgid "Plotting focal mechanisms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:24
msgid ""
"Focal mechanisms can be plotted as beachballs with the :meth:`pygmt.Figure."
"meca` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:26
msgid ""
"The focal mechanism data or parameters can be provided as various input "
"types: ASCII file, :class:`numpy.array`, dictionary, or :class:`pandas."
"Dataframe`. Different conventions to define the focal mechanism are "
"supported: Aki and Richards (``\"aki\"``), global CMT (``\"gcmt\"``), moment "
"tensor (``\"mt\"``), partial focal mechanism (``\"partial\"``), and, "
"principal axis (``\"principal_axis\"``). Please refer to the table in the "
"documentation of :meth:`pygmt.Figure.meca` regarding how to set up the input "
"data in respect to the chosen input type and convention (i.e., the expected "
"column order, keys, or column names). In this tutorial we focus on how to "
"adjust the display of the beachballs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:38
msgid ""
"import pandas as pd\n"
"import pygmt\n"
"from pygmt.params import Pattern\n"
"\n"
"# Set up arguments for basemap\n"
"region = [-5, 5, -5, 5]\n"
"projection = \"X10c/4c\"\n"
"frame = [\"af\", \"+ggray90\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:54
msgid "Setting up the focal mechanism data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:56
msgid ""
"We store focal mechanism parameters for two single events in dictionaries "
"using the moment tensor and Aki and Richards conventions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:61
msgid ""
"# moment tensor convention\n"
"mt_single = {\n"
"    \"mrr\": 4.71,\n"
"    \"mtt\": 0.0381,\n"
"    \"mff\": -4.74,\n"
"    \"mrt\": 0.399,\n"
"    \"mrf\": -0.805,\n"
"    \"mtf\": -1.23,\n"
"    \"exponent\": 24,\n"
"}\n"
"# Aki and Richards convention\n"
"aki_single = {\"strike\": 318, \"dip\": 89, \"rake\": -179, \"magnitude\": "
"7.75}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:82
msgid "Plotting a single beachball"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:84
msgid ""
"Required parameters are ``spec`` and ``scale`` as well as ``longitude``, "
"``latitude`` (event location), and depth (if these values are not included "
"in the argument passed to ``spec``). Additionally, the ``convention`` "
"parameter is required if ``spec`` is an 1-D or 2-D numpy array; for the "
"input types dictionary and ``pandas.Dataframe``, the focal mechanism "
"convention is automatically determined from dictionary keys or :class:"
"`pandas.DataFrame` column names. The ``scale`` parameter controls the radius "
"of the beachball. By default, the value defines the size for a magnitude of "
"5 (i.e., a scalar seismic moment of :math:`M_0 = 4.0 \\times 10^{23}` dyn "
"cm) and the beachball size is proportional to the magnitude. Append "
"``\"+l\"`` to force the radius to be proportional to the seismic moment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:97
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(region=region, projection=projection, frame=frame)\n"
"\n"
"fig.meca(spec=mt_single, scale=\"1c\", longitude=0, latitude=0, depth=0)\n"
"\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:112
msgid "Plotting the components of a seismic moment tensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:114
msgid ""
"A moment tensor can be decomposed into isotropic and deviatoric parts. The "
"deviatoric part can be further decomposed into multiple parts (e.g., a "
"double couple (DC) and a compensated linear vector dipole (CLVD)). Use the "
"``component`` parameter to specify the component you want to plot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:121
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(region=region, projection=projection, frame=frame)\n"
"\n"
"for component, longitude in zip([\"full\", \"dc\", \"deviatoric\"], [-2, 0, "
"2], strict=True):\n"
"    fig.meca(\n"
"        spec=mt_single,\n"
"        scale=\"1c\",\n"
"        longitude=longitude,\n"
"        latitude=0,\n"
"        depth=0,\n"
"        component=component,\n"
"    )\n"
"\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:144
msgid "Filling the quadrants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:146
msgid ""
"Use the parameters ``compression_fill`` and ``extension_fill`` to fill the "
"quadrants with different colors or :class:`patterns <pygmt.params.Pattern>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:151
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(region=region, projection=projection, frame=frame)\n"
"\n"
"fig.meca(\n"
"    spec=mt_single,\n"
"    scale=\"1c\",\n"
"    longitude=-2,\n"
"    latitude=0,\n"
"    depth=0,\n"
"    compression_fill=\"darkorange\",\n"
"    extension_fill=\"cornsilk\",\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"fig.meca(\n"
"    spec=mt_single,\n"
"    scale=\"1c\",\n"
"    longitude=2,\n"
"    latitude=0,\n"
"    depth=0,\n"
"    compression_fill=Pattern(8),\n"
"    extension_fill=Pattern(31),\n"
"    outline=True,\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:184
msgid "Adjusting the outlines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:186
msgid ""
"Use the parameters ``pen`` and ``outline`` for adjusting the circumference "
"of the beachball or all lines (i.e, circumference and both nodal planes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:191
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(region=region, projection=projection, frame=frame)\n"
"\n"
"fig.meca(\n"
"    spec=aki_single,\n"
"    scale=\"1c\",\n"
"    longitude=-2,\n"
"    latitude=0,\n"
"    depth=0,\n"
"    # Use a 1-point thick, darkorange and solid line\n"
"    pen=\"1p,darkorange\",\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"fig.meca(\n"
"    spec=aki_single,\n"
"    scale=\"1c\",\n"
"    longitude=2,\n"
"    latitude=0,\n"
"    depth=0,\n"
"    outline=\"1p,darkorange\",\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:223
msgid "Highlighting the nodal planes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:225
msgid ""
"Use the parameter ``nodal`` to highlight specific nodal planes. ``\"0\"`` "
"refers to both, ``\"1\"`` to the first, and ``\"2\"`` to the second nodal "
"plane(s). Only the circumference and the specified nodal plane(s) are "
"plotted, i.e. the quadrants remain unfilled (transparent). We can make use "
"of the stacking concept of (Py)GMT, and use ``nodal`` in combination with "
"the ``outline``, ``compression_fill`` / ``extension_fill`` and ``pen`` "
"parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:234
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(region=region, projection=projection, frame=frame)\n"
"\n"
"fig.meca(\n"
"    spec=aki_single,\n"
"    scale=\"1c\",\n"
"    longitude=-2,\n"
"    latitude=0,\n"
"    depth=0,\n"
"    nodal=\"0/1p,black\",\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"# Plot the same beachball three times with different settings:\n"
"# (i) Fill the compressive quadrants\n"
"# (ii) Plot the first nodal plane and the circumference in darkorange\n"
"# (iii) Plot the circumference in black on top; use \"-\" to not fill the "
"quadrants\n"
"for kwargs in [\n"
"    {\"compression_fill\": \"lightorange\"},\n"
"    {\"nodal\": \"1/1p,darkorange\"},\n"
"    {\"compression_fill\": \"-\", \"extension_fill\": \"-\", \"pen\": \"1p,"
"gray30\"},\n"
"]:\n"
"    fig.meca(\n"
"        spec=aki_single,\n"
"        scale=\"1c\",\n"
"        longitude=0,\n"
"        latitude=0,\n"
"        depth=0,\n"
"        **kwargs,\n"
"    )\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:273
msgid "Adding offset from event location"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:275
msgid ""
"Specify the optional parameters ``plot_longitude`` and ``plot_latitude``. If "
"``spec`` is an ASCII file with columns for ``plot_longitude`` and "
"``plot_latitude``, the ``offset`` parameter has to be set to ``True``. "
"Besides just drawing a line between the beachball and the event location, a "
"small circle can be plotted at the event location by appending **+s** and "
"the desired circle diameter. The connecting line as well as the outline of "
"the circle are plotted with the  setting of pen, or can be adjusted "
"separately. The fill of the small circle corresponds to the fill of the "
"compressive quadrants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:286
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(region=region, projection=projection, frame=frame)\n"
"\n"
"fig.meca(\n"
"    spec=aki_single,\n"
"    scale=\"1c\",\n"
"    longitude=-1,\n"
"    latitude=0,\n"
"    depth=0,\n"
"    plot_longitude=-3,\n"
"    plot_latitude=2,\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"fig.meca(\n"
"    spec=aki_single,\n"
"    scale=\"1c\",\n"
"    longitude=3,\n"
"    latitude=0,\n"
"    depth=0,\n"
"    plot_longitude=1,\n"
"    plot_latitude=2,\n"
"    offset=\"+p1p,darkorange+s0.25c\",\n"
"    compression_fill=\"lightorange\",\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:321
msgid "Plotting multiple beachballs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:323
msgid ""
"Now we want to plot multiple beachballs with one call of :meth:`pygmt.Figure."
"meca`. We use data of four earthquakes taken from USGS. For each focal "
"mechanism parameter a list with a length corresponding to the number of "
"events has to be given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:329
msgid ""
"# Set up a pandas.DataFrame with multiple focal mechanism parameters.\n"
"aki_multiple = pd.DataFrame(\n"
"    {\n"
"        \"strike\": [255, 173, 295, 318],\n"
"        \"dip\": [70, 68, 79, 89],\n"
"        \"rake\": [20, 83, -177, -179],\n"
"        \"magnitude\": [7.0, 5.8, 6.0, 7.8],\n"
"        \"longitude\": [-72.53, -79.61, 69.46, 37.01],\n"
"        \"latitude\": [18.44, 0.90, 33.02, 37.23],\n"
"        \"depth\": [13, 19, 4, 10],\n"
"        \"plot_longitude\": [-70, -110, 100, 0],\n"
"        \"plot_latitude\": [40, 10, 50, 55],\n"
"        \"event_name\": [\n"
"            \"Haiti - 2010/01/12\",\n"
"            \"Esmeraldas - 2022/03/27\",\n"
"            \"Afghanistan - 2022/06/21\",\n"
"            \"Syria/Turkey - 2023/02/06\",\n"
"        ],\n"
"    }\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:358
msgid "Adding a label"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:360
msgid ""
"Use the optional parameter ``event_name`` to add a label near the beachball, "
"e.g., event name or event date and time. Change the font of the label text "
"by appending **+f** and the desired font (size,name,color) to the argument "
"passed to the ``scale`` parameter. Additionally, the location of the label "
"relative to the beachball [Default is ``\"TC\"``, i.e., Top Center] can be "
"changed by appending **+j** and an offset can be applied by appending **+o** "
"with values for *dx*\\ /*dy*. Add a colored [Default is white] box behind "
"the label via the parameter ``label_box``. Force a fixed size of the "
"beachball by appending **+m** to the argument passed to the ``scale`` "
"parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:371
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.coast(region=\"d\", projection=\"N10c\", land=\"lightgray\", "
"frame=True)\n"
"\n"
"fig.meca(spec=aki_multiple, scale=\"0.4c+m+f5p\", label_box=\"white@30\", "
"offset=\"+s0.1c\")\n"
"\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:386
msgid "Using size-coding and color-coding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:388
msgid ""
"The beachball can be sized and colored by the quantities given as "
"``magnitude`` and ``depth``, e.g., by moment magnitude or hypocentral depth, "
"respectively. Use the parameter ``cmap`` to pass the desired colormap. Now, "
"the fills of the small circles indicating the event locations are given by "
"the colormap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/focal_mechanisms.rst:395
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.coast(region=\"d\", projection=\"N10c\", land=\"lightgray\", "
"frame=True)\n"
"\n"
"# Set up colormap and colorbar for hypocentral depth\n"
"pygmt.makecpt(cmap=\"SCM/lajolla\", series=[0, 20])\n"
"fig.colorbar(label=\"Hypocentral depth\", unit=\"km\")\n"
"\n"
"fig.meca(\n"
"    spec=aki_multiple,\n"
"    scale=\"0.4c+f5p\",\n"
"    offset=\"0.2p,gray30+s0.1c\",\n"
"    label_box=\"white@30\",\n"
"    cmap=True,\n"
"    outline=\"0.2p,gray30\",\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

